  "abstract_summary": "An agent that carries memory across tasks is only as good as the entries it keeps. We begin from an observation that is easy to reproduce and uncomfortable for the field: naively accumulating cross-task experience can make an agent \\emph{worse} than one with no memory at all. On AgentBoard, a workflow-induction memo...",
